{#- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    SOBRE IVÁN — rebuilt September 10, 2026 from a CV into a short memoir.

    🔑 The order is the whole change: **help is the plot, races are the
    evidence.** It opens on the friend who wanted a marathon and closes on the
    roster; the twenty marathons sit in the MIDDLE so they cannot impersonate
    the thesis. What it replaced put a four-figure brag bar (20 / 3 / +100 / 46)
    second on the page and then three essays that repeated the same PRs.

    🚨 THREE RULES THIS PAGE ENFORCES, and each one is a thing that was on it:
    1. **No stat component at the top. Numbers live inside sentences.**
       `.about-record` and credentials.json's `record` array are retired.
    2. **One ugly number per proud number.** The sub-3 only means something
       beside the 4h15, and the average of the twenty — nearer 3h30 — is the
       sentence an athlete can actually stand next to. Iván confirmed every one
       of these on September 10, 2026; they were not in this repo before.
    3. **TrainingPeaks is a pipe, not a verdict.** The old page said "no es que
       yo diga que soy buen coach, es que la plataforma decide mandarme
       atletas", which denies bragging while doing it. It states the mechanism
       and stops.

    ⚠️ Athlete counts are owned by `monthly-close/YYYY-MM.md`, never by this
    page. "Alrededor de cuarenta" is deliberately rounded and slow-moving so it
    does not need correcting every close: `data/monthly_close/2026-08-roster.csv`
    carries 47 athletes in August, 42 paying, 37 active at month end.
